let md='# Public-persona roster proposals — #139\n\nAll six batches: seventy-two creature mechanics, twelve per colour. This is a creative cast/brief pass, not new game definitions or commissioned images. Mechanical names/IDs/effects/costs/rarities/acquisition remain unchanged; shipping names/silhouettes are proposals. Public-role/source links support the reference, not the invented joke or a claim of familiarity among Danish sixteen-year-olds. Public references were checked on 12 October 2026; thin or inaccessible pages are flagged for verification before art; the satire concerns public work and uses original text.\n\nFollow ART-BIBLE.md and attach approved style-board plus shipped-creature references before generation. Keep dusk/cute-horror contrast, strong dark outlines and the relevant affinity jewel accent; do not paint a realistic human face on an animal. The seven common starter helpers are already integrated under#137 and are separate.\n\n| Mechanical concept / ID | Proposed pun / inspiration | Silhouette and main cue | Joke / mechanic link | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n';
for(const r of rows) md+=`| ${r.workingName} / ${r.mechanicalId} | **${r.proposedName}** / ${r.inspiration} · ${r.rarity} · ${r.acquisition.channel} | ${r.silhouette} ${r.signatureProp} | ${r.jokeAngle} ${r.mechanicLink} | [Public reference](${r.source}) |\n`;
md+='\n## Review and production gates\n\n- All seventy-two preserve their original mechanical contract in persona-roster.json. Familiarity, pun quality, historical Mythic presentation and any helper exception still need review; no source certifies those design choices. No existing public-persona creature has been reissued as a new species.\n- Mechanical IDs remain stable. A proposed animal silhouette/name does not silently merge creature identity with an existing animal, alter two-copy limits or create an alternate-print loophole. Name/asset aliases should be explicit when definitions are released.\n- Inference Heron remains the proposed Town Hall story-only reward even when its shipping pun changes. No cast choice admits a plot card into packs.\n- Theorem Tortoise still has its existing #109/Fate gates. No historical figure bypasses replay/expiry/Win/save policy. Rarity belongs to the mechanical release, not our admiration for the public figure.\n- One shared introduction voice per reviewed released creature can come before optional attack/defeat barks. Exact runtime lines/hosts enter existing source and tools/voices.mjs plan only at implementation; no audio requests, logos, copied quotations or recordings in this pass.\n\nAll six colour batches are authored. Next: review recognisability/pun/prop choices and thin-source flags, then small balance-approved release batches. Do not overwrite reviewed proposals without noting the revision. Check the full cast for recognisable jokes, distinct silhouettes, colour coverage and existing-actor overlaps before future art.\n';
md+='\n## Voice and existing sound keys\n\nOriginal delivery directions and exact sharedSfx arrays are also in persona-roster.json. Shared sound names below are existing data/sfx.js keys. They are candidates to select at the actual action, not instructions to play them together; voice-direction phrases such as “summon” or “paper” describe an impression, not new sound keys. No new audio generation is requested.\n\n| Proposed creature | Original voice direction | Reusable SFX keys |\n|---|---|---|\n';
for(const r of rows)md+=`| ${r.proposedName} | ${r.voiceDirection} | ${r.sharedSfx.join(', ')} |\n`;
